WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.601
-You want to talk about
strategy because you...

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:03.703
-Yes. Yes.

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.104
-Again, you called this
last time.

00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:08.207
And talk about what happened
in Michigan in 2018 and --

00:00:08.207 --> 00:00:09.409
-Last November, we --

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:13.812
Michigan sadly went red
for Trump in 2016.

00:00:13.812 --> 00:00:16.749
But this past November,
we brought it back to blue.

00:00:16.749 --> 00:00:18.584
And we kicked out
all the Republicans

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:20.687
in the state capitol
and we got the governor,

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:23.222
lieutenant-governor, attorney
general, secretary of state,

00:00:23.222 --> 00:00:27.026
and we kicked out
two Republicans, Congressmen,

00:00:27.026 --> 00:00:29.629
in suburban Detroit --
in suburban Detroit --

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:31.731
and replaced them with
two Democratic women.

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.299
So Michigan is now back --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:35.901
Let me tell you how we did it.
Here's how we did it.

00:00:35.901 --> 00:00:37.737
Amd we got to do this
in states --

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:39.772
especially the swing states
next year.

00:00:39.772 --> 00:00:43.943
Ballot proposals brought out
the people to vote last November

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.611
who may not have voted.

00:00:45.611 --> 00:00:48.748
So we came up with this idea.
Let's get two ballot proposals.

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:51.084
Actually, this is Karl Rove's
and Bush's idea.

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:54.654
In 2004, they got 14 states
to put an amendment

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:57.757
on the ballot proposal
to ban gay marriage,

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:59.626
and it passed
in all 14 states,

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:02.928
and it brought out enough people
to get Bush elected.

00:01:02.928 --> 00:01:04.564
We can do this this time.

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:06.733
If we put ballot measures
on the ballots.

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:09.502
We did it in Michigan with
with marijuana legalization,

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:11.704
we doubled the youth vote...
-Yeah.

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:14.574
-...from the previous
off-year election.

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:17.710
And -- and the African-American
vote,

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:20.946
which thousands had sat it out
in '16,

00:01:20.946 --> 00:01:23.182
unhappy with the choices,

00:01:23.182 --> 00:01:25.018
came back to vote
last November

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:27.453
because we had a ballot proposal

00:01:27.453 --> 00:01:31.390
to make gerrymandering
and voter suppression illegal,

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:32.792
and it passed.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:35.795
It passed, marijuana passed,
and we had a huge

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:38.865
African-American turnout,
and that gave us --

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:41.067
we got Democrats elected off it.

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:45.438
So instead of putting all
our hopes in one politician

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:48.641
to carry the thing, we have to
get these ballot proposals on

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.075
in the swing states.

00:01:50.075 --> 00:01:52.145
That will bring out people
to vote.

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:54.314
Now, I tweeted at Trump

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:55.848
just before I came out
to watch tonight.

00:01:55.848 --> 00:01:57.283
-Oh, wow. Okay, gotcha.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.885
-You know, because I was
going to tell him, you know --

00:01:59.885 --> 00:02:03.055
You think he is --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.055 --> 00:02:05.625
He's like -- I told --

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:07.993
-Thank you.

00:02:07.993 --> 00:02:10.530
-I told him to get
a bucket of KFC.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.897
-Yep.

00:02:11.897 --> 00:02:14.032
-And he's in his robe right now
watching you and I.

00:02:14.032 --> 00:02:15.501
-Yeah, probably, yeah.

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:18.805
-And I said, you got to watch
because I'm going to tell you

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:21.508
how we're going remove you
from the White House next year.

00:02:21.508 --> 00:02:22.775
-All right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:24.777
-And we're gonna do it --
we're gonna do it

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:27.880
by getting those ballot
proposals in those states

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:31.551
to bring out the majority
of Americans, or that 70% --

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:33.786
women, people of color,
young adults.

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:36.088
We're going to run
a beloved candidate

00:02:36.088 --> 00:02:37.723
who is a street fighter.

00:02:37.723 --> 00:02:39.291
All right, I'm serious.

00:02:39.291 --> 00:02:43.596
Folks, if we put up
the wrong horse in this race,

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:45.264
we are doomed again.

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:46.599
Let's not do that.

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.367
And I'm willing to say --
okay, so let's say --

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:51.070
Obviously I love Bernie
and his politics and all that,

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:53.939
but we all have to agree
we're going to all vote

00:02:53.939 --> 00:02:56.542
for the person that isn't
just going to beat Trump,

00:02:56.542 --> 00:02:58.144
'cause I think there's
four or five candidates now

00:02:58.144 --> 00:02:59.545
that could beat him.

00:02:59.545 --> 00:03:01.581
But beating isn't good enough.
Hillary beat him.

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:03.549
We have to crush Trump.

00:03:03.549 --> 00:03:05.885
It has to be orange crush.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:08.588
Orange crush.
Operation Orange Crush --

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:10.155
I just came up with that.
-There you go.

00:03:10.155 --> 00:03:11.590
Well, you got to
come back again.

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:13.726
We'll check in on the operation.
That's Michael Moore, everybody.

